          <p>
            The table makes the shape of this market plain. Three of the five are 700-watt, 0.7 cubic foot machines, and the honest truth is that they cook almost identically. The differences between them are in the control panel layout, the finish, the door and the brand's parts support, which is why we rank them on fit and usability rather than pretending one 700-watt magnetron is meaningfully better than another.
