            The Panasonic is the outlier on purpose. At 1.2 cubic feet it is not a small microwave, but it is the most widely sold inverter microwave in the US, and it is the right comparison point for anyone wondering whether inverter technology is worth the extra size and price. For dorms and RVs it is usually too big. For a small kitchen with a real counter, it can be the better buy.
